{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles","id":302506,"title":"Rules Questions: Iron Skin, Multiple Styles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-04T12:10:45-08:00","id":302506,"title":"Rules Questions: Iron Skin, Multiple Styles","content":"Does Iron Skin (the merit) stack with other forms of armor on a Vampire? The merit only applies to bashing attacks, but swords and bullets both deal bashing to vampires now. It's specifically noted that characters with supernatural armor - with a werewolf's hide being used as an example - can stack that armor with normal armor... except Iron skin isn't supernatural armor inherently, though it might be on a vampire. It's &quot;natural&quot; armor that might &quot;become&quot; supernatural with the Embrace, so I'm not sure what to do with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can characters benefit from multiple Styles simultaneously?<br /> <br /> The easiest example is physical conflict: If I've got Martial Arts 5 and Street Fighting 2, can my successful unarmed attack with hands as +2L weapons, per Martial Arts 5, also cause my opponent to take a -1 penalty on his next action, per Street Fighting 2?<br /> <br /> Obviously there are some things that clearly can't be used together - can't spend WP on multiple things or sacrificing defense multiple times, etc. But there is a LOT of room where mechanically, I can see multiple styles applying. Some make quite fine thematic sense, too. (Kindred Dueling and Light Weapons, Ride the Wave and Martial Arts / Street Fighting, etc). <br /> <br /> With the social styles (Etiquette and Fast-Talking) there's lots room for combination as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:18:11-08:00","id":302574,"title":"","content":"No to both.<br /> <br /> Iron Skin - thematically, the damage is the same, the vampire simply does not care so much about it. So if Iron Skin helps a human - it helps a vampire. Otherwise, you'll need something better.<br /> Characters cannot stacks style maneuver's unless they specifically say otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:24:36-08:00","id":302601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=302574#post302574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters cannot stacks style maneuver's unless they specifically say otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page number or errata link for this? I could only find the clause about Defense Sacrifice:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> GMC p175: Many Fighting Style Merits require a character to sacrifice their Defense. Defense cannot be sacrificed multiple times in a turn; this prevents <b>certain </b>maneuvers from being used together. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:32:12-08:00","id":302606,"title":"","content":"Well, I think simple logic applies here: If I'm hitting you with a karate strike, I can't be punching you with a boxer punch as well. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, whole fighting system breaks apart, as instead of having a cap on your capabilities (max stats + 1 maneuver (or more, in some circumstances, where this is permitted)) you can go to infinity and beyond.. and much cheaper than actually increasing your stats, as usually buying a Dot in Fighting Style gives more benefits then buying a Skill dot in Fighting Skill. <br /> <br /> Anyways, I think someone more accustomed to the books will find the passage. But if some player tries to go with &quot;I can apply these several different maneuvers, because there's nowhere else which forbids it&quot;, I'd think that he's just horrendously power gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:35:51-08:00","id":302609,"title":"","content":"I agree on the power level problem, which is why I want the quote. Because unfortunately in a mechanical rules sense, I can only find the above clause, which is then further reinforced by some maneuvers which state they cannot be combined with <i>specific </i>other maneuvers. Which from a logical standpoint means the non-combination is the exception, not the norm. Obviously common sense will rule the day, but that also means if the player can make a case on how the two maneuvers could overlap, they can still make the case. The case is closed if there is the only-one-maneuver rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:40:56-08:00","id":302610,"title":"","content":"Or you can close the case, under the basis that only maneuvers from the same fighting style can be stacked, if the said maneuver says so. (since, some of them makes it so). Further then, you can say, that, the same way one character cannot drive two cars at once (baring extremely ridiculous circumstances) so does fighting in one Fighting Style, bar you from Fighting in Another. There's no need to spell it out. <br /> <br /> And once again, if your player is making &quot;cases&quot; like that, I'd say, that he's just trying to power game his way into it, and that his character perfectly fits with using just one of those maneuvers at once. If he wants more power, suggest investing in skills. If he wants more utility, then he can get more different fighting styles... in which case he can use only one at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:42:20-08:00","id":302611,"title":"","content":"And I guess I'm wrong. Armory Reloaded, Page 62 talks about this, and permits usage of different maneuvers at once, as long as they don't require same costs.<br /> But imo, that's just stupid. I'll be banning them, since there's no character concept which requires stackage of several, and all it accomplishes is gives some more power gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:44:23-08:00","id":302616,"title":"","content":"The most common interpretation I see is that your passive Style maneuvers are always active and always apply, if they make sense. So yes, if one is a master martial artist with lots of experience in street brawls, too, your maneuvers would stack. It makes sense to me. Such a person would be very dangerous in a fight.<br /> <br /> Usually, active maneuvers are kind of all-or-nothing, especially the ones that sacrifice Defense, so it wouldn't make a lot of sense for most of them to be used together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:48:07-08:00","id":302640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=302611#post302611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I guess I'm wrong. Armory Reloaded, Page 62 talks about this, and permits usage of different maneuvers at once, as long as they don't require same costs.<br /> But imo, that's just stupid. I'll be banning them, since there's no character concept which requires stackage of several, and all it accomplishes is gives some more power gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was rooting for you! I'll probably say that maneuvers can be combined with a good case, <b>and when</b> they don't seem broken in play. We've got a good precedent where the ST can make rulings like that, and the player is free to swap out the affected traits free of charge, so I'm not concerned about a fight. Usually it's clear when something's OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:21:34-08:00","id":302690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=302616#post302616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most common interpretation I see is that your passive Style maneuvers are always active and always apply, if they make sense. So yes, if one is a master martial artist with lots of experience in street brawls, too, your maneuvers would stack. It makes sense to me. Such a person would be very dangerous in a fight.<br /> <br /> Usually, active maneuvers are kind of all-or-nothing, especially the ones that sacrifice Defense, so it wouldn't make a lot of sense for most of them to be used together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what I've always ruled in my games. It is balanced, as far as I can tell. Expensive though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:27:31-08:00","id":302692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=302611#post302611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I guess I'm wrong. Armory Reloaded, Page 62 talks about this, and permits usage of different maneuvers at once, as long as they don't require same costs.<br /> But imo, that's just stupid. I'll be banning them, since there's no character concept which requires stackage of several, and all it accomplishes is gives some more power gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find it to be &quot;power gaming&quot; or unbalanced at all, really. If someone has taken the time to master Martial Arts and Street Fighting or whatever, that's a character who is literally one of the most lethal hand-to-hand fighters in the world. Yes, they're dangerous, but that's the point. If Jackie Chan is going all-out trying to kill you, he sure as heck is going to <i>seem </i>broken when you're on the other side of that! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:00:18-08:00","id":302754,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input, folks. Hope we can get an &quot;official&quot; response soon, maybe even get this added to the FAQ!<br /> <br /> I could see the &quot;stacking styles&quot; even for passive bonuses being a balance problem in some cases, but I think it's more of a danger in a mortal-focused game where the primary combat skill has been maxed out and buying merits becomes more xp-efficient than putting more dots into attributes. That's typically no longer the case once you've opened up the supernatural powers menu.<br /> <br /> If it became a real problem, I'd suggest creating a &quot;hybrid style&quot; merit or something, where each dot in the merit allowed you to combine stuff from a single other style. So 2-dots of Hybrid style would be needed to get the passive bonuses from 2 styles at the same time, etc. Unless there's some blatantly unbalanced combination of passive abilities I'm missing (entirely possible), that'd at least move the xp-efficiency way down compared to alternatives - which seems to be the main complaint I've seen so far.<br /> <br /> I've yet to see a Style+Style combination that's as powerful as Style + PT5, anyway. (But PT5 is le broken.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:26:15-08:00","id":302771,"title":"","content":"<b>@wampa:</b> Remember that Style merits work a little differently from normal merits; you have to buy each level of the merit individually (almost as if if they were 3 to 5 different Merits that require each-other.)<br /> <br /> To buy all 5 levels of Martial Arts and the first 2 levels of Street Fighting would cost a total of 18 xp. Now ask yourself, &quot;does spending 18 xp to get a 2L weapon that gives my opponent a -1 penalty to one roll (that I have no real control over) <i>really</i> broken compared to, say, a gun?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think you'll find that no, it isn't.<br /> <br /> Plus, US Army basic training would be best represented with a combination of Martial Arts and Street Fighting, if we're coming up with examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T18:51:28-08:00","id":302848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=302771#post302771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@wampa:</b> Remember that Style merits work a little differently from normal merits; you have to buy each level of the merit individually (almost as if if they were 3 to 5 different Merits that require each-other.)</div> </div> </div> </div> As far as I was aware, it takes 5 xp to get Street Fighting 5. Can you give me a page number where it's stated they're purchased differently than other merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:14:32-08:00","id":302854,"title":"","content":"P. 158:<br /> <br /> Merits marked as Style Merits allow access to specialized<br /> maneuvers. Each maneuver is a prerequisite for the next in its<br /> sequence. So if a Style Merit has a three-dot maneuver and a<br /> four-dot maneuver, you must purchase the three-dot version<br /> before accessing the four-dot.<br /> <br /> At least, I read that as costing 1xp for the first, 2xp for the second, etc, etc. That's how it worked in 1e, so I'm assuming that's what they meant here (I hope a dev can clarify.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:18:26-08:00","id":302855,"title":"","content":"I allow vampires to benefit from Iron Skin (and let it &quot;stack&quot;), but only in cases that would cause bashing damage to a human. <br /> <br /> And Amechra: That's just legacy language that crept in. Sorry. It costs 5 Experiences to get all five dots of a Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:50:34-08:00","id":302910,"title":"","content":"Oh, OK.<br /> <br /> I've gotta tell my two players with Parkour that they have 3 levels instead of 2.<br /> <br /> I still think allowing Fighting Style merits to synergize is good clean fun, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T00:14:16-08:00","id":303039,"title":"","content":"It is good clean fun. I've been using multiple Fighting Styles to represent MMA characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0y