by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=303385#post303385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I read that as simply stating you couldn't spend 1xp to cherry pick the dots in the merit you wanted. For example, with Martial Arts, I couldn't just buy the 5th dot in the style for 1xp.<br /> <br /> Dev clarification would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am with you on this. That you cant hand pick the abilities. all merits are 1 exp per dot. The Merit is called Martial Arts Style ( example ) If i spend 3 exp I get the 1 2 and 3 abilities listed within it. The things listed arent the merits they are just what happens when you get the dots in said merit. now later if I want to spend 1 more exp I put it n Martial arts Style and get the 4th dot ability. Think of it like Majesty. I put 3 dots in that and I think Awe, Confidant and Green eyes. I dont write them all separately as different disciplines. I hope that this explaination was not confusing ^.^ <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:18:26-08:00","id":427957,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm surprised nobody brought up the example given of using two styles simultaneously. You can use Shiv and Martial Arts or Shiv and Street Fighting. You can only attack once a turn. You can only sacrifice defense once a turn. Many Styles have requirements to use them which exclude other Styles. Without an example to the contrary, I think it remains balanced. Seems to me stacked maneuvers would generally be used during grappling, close combat, or melee with weapons that deal light damage. A master of any of those types of combat would be stacking like crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T16:21:00-08:00","id":428258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/302506-rules-questions-iron-skin-multiple-styles?p=303385#post303385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read that as simply stating you couldn't spend 1xp to cherry pick the dots in the merit you wanted. For example, with Martial Arts, I couldn't just buy the 5th dot in the style for 1xp.<br /> <br /> Dev clarification would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave H. just said it costs 5 experiences to buy 5 dots in a style. First post on this page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid